## Archive Cleanup Policy

When creating a new handover, after archiving:

1. List files in `.cursor/handover-archive/`
2. If more than 30 archived handovers exist, delete the oldest files to maintain only 30
3. Report how many archives were cleaned up (if any)

## When to Update Handover

- **After docs or versions change:** If you update documentation or tool versions that affect session continuity (e.g. PRD, technology stack, key paths), update `.cursor/rules/abase-handover-context.mdc` so the next session has accurate context.
- **Recording solutions:** Recording errors and their solutions (e.g. in a `docs/SOLUTIONS.md` or similar) helps handover and future reference; mention such a log in the handover if the project uses one.

## Usage Examples

Example user requests that may trigger handover creation (actual wording may vary):

- "Create a handover document"
- "Prepare session handover"
- "Create handover" / "Create handover-context"
- "I'm ending this session, create a handover"
- "Handover please"

Use judgment to recognize when the user is requesting a session handover, even if phrased differently.

## Notes

- The live handover content is **`.cursor/rules/abase-handover-context.mdc`** with `alwaysApply: true`, so Cursor loads it automatically; no explicit read at session start is needed.
- This rule (`handover-management.mdc`) has `alwaysApply: true` so the agent always has the instructions above.
- Timestamps use local time without timezone suffix.
- The archive (`.cursor/handover-archive/`) keeps history of previous handovers for reference.
